# Database
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_USER=root
DB_PASS=
DB_NAME=campusphere_db

# Server
PORT=3000
SESSION_SECRET=change_this_to_a_long_random_string

# Google OAuth (Web application client; redirect URI must match Google Cloud console)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/callback

# Registration trust policy (Milestone 8, Section 8.6):
#   - Local email/password POST /register is GUEST-ONLY (non-guest roles rejected).
#   - student-cspc / instructor self-registration requires verified Google OAuth
#     domains (@my.cspc.edu.ph -> student, @cspc.edu.ph -> instructor).
#   - Admin creation remains seed/admin-only (never self-registerable).
#   - Supabase defense in depth: migration 0009 makes app_create_local_user
#     guest-only. Apply database/supabase/0009_*.sql in the Supabase SQL editor.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seed strict-constraint mode (R8 identity/profile uniqueness)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# database/seed.js adds MySQL UNIQUE keys for one-profile-per-user and unique
# non-null (oauth_provider, oauth_subject) pairs. On an existing database that
# already contains duplicate identity rows it normally SKIPS the affected key
# with a warning so local/dev seeding stays non-destructive and idempotent.
#
# For deployment / production setup, set this to true (or 1) so the seed instead
# FAILS HARD (exits nonzero) when a duplicate would block a constraint — forcing
# the duplicates to be resolved before release. Strict mode is also implied when
# NODE_ENV=production. Defaults to off (lenient) when unset.
#
# SEED_STRICT_CONSTRAINTS=true

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limiting (Milestone 8, Section 8.3)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fixed-window limiter (middleware/rateLimit.js). All values below are
# optional; the conservative defaults shown keep the seeded defense/demo flow
# usable. *_MAX = requests per window; *_WINDOW_MS = window length in ms. There
# is intentionally no "disable all rate limits" switch.
#
# WHERE the counters live is chosen by the runtime, not by these variables
# (M12.P1-R4, services/rateLimitStore.js):
#   - Local development / container rehearsal: an in-memory fixed-window Map,
#     single process. No Upstash configuration and no RATE_LIMIT_KEY_SECRET is
#     required, and the Upstash package is never even loaded.
#   - Vercel (VERCEL=1): a SHARED Upstash Redis counter incremented by ONE
#     atomic server-side script. Vercel runs many independent instances, so a
#     process-local Map would let each instance keep its own counter and
#     multiply the effective limit. See the Vercel section near the bottom of
#     this file for the three required server-only variables.
# The limits, windows, bucket scopes, fixed 429 body, and Retry-After contract
# are identical in both modes.
#
# Auth form preflight (per IP, pre-body): POST /login /register
# /auth/complete-registration /logout
# RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_MAX=20
# RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_WINDOW_MS=900000
#
# Login account bucket (per hashed email + IP): POST /login
# RATE_LIMIT_LOGIN_ACCOUNT_MAX=8
# RATE_LIMIT_LOGIN_ACCOUNT_WINDOW_MS=900000
#
# OAuth start/callback (per IP): GET /auth/google /auth/callback
# RATE_LIMIT_OAUTH_MAX=20
# RATE_LIMIT_OAUTH_WINDOW_MS=600000
#
# Profile update (per logged-in user + IP): POST /api/update-profile
# RATE_LIMIT_PROFILE_MAX=20
# RATE_LIMIT_PROFILE_WINDOW_MS=600000
#
# Admin mutations (per admin user + IP): unsafe /admin/api/* methods
# RATE_LIMIT_ADMIN_MUTATION_MAX=80
# RATE_LIMIT_ADMIN_MUTATION_WINDOW_MS=300000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session store + cookie/proxy policy (Milestone 8, Section 8.4;
# Milestone 9, Section 9.4: Supabase is the preferred production session store)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SESSION_STORE — where express-session persists sessions.
#   supabase -> persistent Supabase/PostgreSQL store (services/supabaseSessionStore.js,
#               table public.app_sessions). PREFERRED production/demo store. Requires
#               SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (below) AND migration
#               database/supabase/0011_supabase_session_store.sql applied.
#   mysql    -> persistent MySQL store (services/mysqlSessionStore.js, table
#               app_sessions, via the DB_* pool). Fallback / local-rehearsal store.
#   memory   -> in-memory MemoryStore. LOCAL-DEVELOPMENT ONLY (not shared across
#               processes, lost on restart). In production, SESSION_STORE=memory
#               FAILS startup (fail-closed), as does any unknown value.
# Defaults: production -> supabase, non-production -> memory.
# Recommended for production/demo:
# SESSION_STORE=supabase
#
# SESSION_SECRET — signs the session cookie. In production it MUST be set, be at
# least 32 chars, and NOT be a known placeholder ("change_this_to_a_long_random_string"
# or "campusphere_fallback_secret"); otherwise the server refuses to start.
# Non-production falls back to an insecure dev secret with a warning if unset.
#
# SESSION_SECRET_PREVIOUS — optional comma-separated list of OLD secrets, kept
# only so cookies signed with a rotated-out secret still verify. The CURRENT
# SESSION_SECRET signs all new cookies; previous values only verify old ones.
# In production each previous value must ALSO be non-placeholder and at least 32
# chars (a rotated-out secret still verifies cookies), or the server exits.
# Rotate by moving the old SESSION_SECRET into SESSION_SECRET_PREVIOUS and
# setting a new SESSION_SECRET.
# SESSION_SECRET_PREVIOUS=old-secret-1,old-secret-2
#
# SESSION_COOKIE_MAX_AGE_MS — optional positive integer cookie lifetime in ms
# (default 86400000 = 24h). Invalid value: fails startup in production, ignored
# with a warning in non-production.
# SESSION_COOKIE_MAX_AGE_MS=86400000
#
# Cookie policy (not individually configurable): httpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Path=/,
# no Domain. Name + Secure depend on NODE_ENV:
#   production  -> name "__Host-campusphere.sid", Secure=true (requires HTTPS).
#   development -> name "campusphere.sid", Secure=false.
#
# TRUST_PROXY — non-negative integer of proxy hops to trust (express "trust
# proxy"). Production default 1; non-production default 0. Invalid value fails
# startup in production, ignored with a warning in non-production. In production
# behind TLS termination, the proxy MUST forward X-Forwarded-Proto=https so the
# Secure __Host- cookie is issued.
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth / Profile runtime data source switch  (Milestone 2, Section 2.2)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selects which backend the auth / profile / dashboard / admin-user controllers
# read from. CONSUMED at runtime today (read by config/authDataSource.js); the
# controllers branch to the Supabase repository path when this is "supabase".
#
# Allowed values:
#   mysql     -> existing direct MySQL queries (default, also the fallback).
#   supabase  -> Supabase repository path (final runtime target).
#
# Defaults to "mysql" when unset, empty, or set to an unrecognised value.
# Switching to "supabase" requires the SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# values below to be configured.
#
# AUTH_DATA_SOURCE=mysql

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Map / Buildings / Routes runtime switches  (Milestone 3, Section 3.3)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Independent switches for the campus-map migration, read by config/mapRuntime.js.
# All three are CONSUMED at runtime today (the building/route controllers and the
# map views branch on them).
#
# BUILDING_DATA_SOURCE — backend for building reads (/buildings, /map, admin).
#   mysql     -> existing direct MySQL queries (default, also the fallback).
#   supabase  -> Supabase repository path.
#
# ROUTE_DATA_SOURCE — backend for search / routes / pathfinding reads.
#   mysql     -> existing direct MySQL queries (default, also the fallback).
#   supabase  -> Supabase repository path.
#
# MAP_RENDERER — which map library the map views render with.
#   leaflet   -> Leaflet / OpenStreetMap map (default / fallback).
#   maplibre  -> MapLibre GL map (the map view loads MapLibre when set).
#
# Each defaults to the value shown above when unset, empty, or unrecognised.
# The "supabase" modes additionally require SUPABASE_URL and
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY below to be configured.
#
# BUILDING_DATA_SOURCE=mysql
# ROUTE_DATA_SOURCE=mysql
# MAP_RENDERER=leaflet

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Content runtime data source switch  (Milestone 4, Section 4.3)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selects which backend the dashboard / events / admin-content (news, events,
# FAQs, settings) controllers read from. CONSUMED at runtime today (read by
# config/contentDataSource.js); controllers branch to the Supabase repository
# path when this is "supabase".
#
# Allowed values:
#   mysql     -> existing direct MySQL queries (default, also the fallback).
#   supabase  -> Supabase repository path.
#
# Defaults to "mysql" when unset, empty, or set to an unrecognised value.
# Switching to "supabase" requires the SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# values below to be configured.
#
# CONTENT_DATA_SOURCE=mysql

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VR runtime data source switch  (Milestone 5, Section 5.2)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selects which backend the VR / 360 controllers (scene browser, guided route
# viewer, and the VR route API) read from. CONSUMED at runtime today (read by
# config/vrDataSource.js); controllers branch to the Supabase repository path
# when this is "supabase".
#
# Allowed values:
#   mysql     -> existing direct MySQL queries (default, also the fallback).
#   supabase  -> Supabase repository path.
#
# Defaults to "mysql" when unset, empty, or set to an unrecognised value.
# Switching to "supabase" requires the server-only SUPABASE_URL and
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY values below to be configured.
#
# VR_DATA_SOURCE=mysql

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Room-schedule runtime data source switch  (Milestone 11, Section 11.4)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selects which backend the room/facility scheduling data access
# (repositories/scheduleRepository.js: admin schedule CRUD and the public
# building schedule display) runs against. CONSUMED at runtime today (read by
# config/scheduleDataSource.js). Schedules are REAL admin-managed room/facility
# data — not SIS, enrollment, or instructor-load simulation.
#
# Allowed values:
#   mysql     -> parameterized MySQL pool queries (default, also the fallback).
#   supabase  -> server-only Supabase repository path.
#
# Defaults to "mysql" when unset, empty, or set to an unrecognised value.
# Switching to "supabase" requires the server-only SUPABASE_URL and
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY values below to be configured, plus owner-applied
# migrations database/supabase/0012_room_schedules.sql and
# database/supabase/0013_vr_hotspot_schedule_metadata.sql when VR room-door
# schedule hotspots are enabled.
#
# SCHEDULE_DATA_SOURCE=mysql

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase / PostgreSQL / PostGIS  (server-only; cloud data target)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONSUMED at runtime by the server-only Supabase client (config/supabase.js)
# and the repositories/ layer whenever any *_DATA_SOURCE switch above is set to
# "supabase". Leaving these blank/unset keeps the app on the MySQL fallback. The
# migrations under database/supabase/ (0001-0019) are applied manually by the
# project owner; see
# docs/deployment.md for env vars and SQL apply order. SESSION_STORE=supabase
# additionally requires migration 0011_supabase_session_store.sql
# (public.app_sessions), and the room-scheduling runtime
# (SCHEDULE_DATA_SOURCE=supabase) requires 0012_room_schedules.sql
# and VR room-door schedule hotspots require 0013_vr_hotspot_schedule_metadata.sql.
# Road-following routing and selected-demo parity require owner-applied
# migrations 0014 through 0019 for the verified graph, path_geometry, atomic
# admin writes, Guard House topology, CAS baseline, and selected-demo parity.
# CampuSphere uses its own graph and owner-managed road geometry; it
# does not call Google Maps, Google Earth, Strava, SIS, or an external router.
#
# WARNING: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is a SERVER-ONLY privileged key. Never
# expose it to EJS templates, anything under public/, browser globals,
# screenshots, or any committed file. Treat it like a database root password.
# Browser reads (if ever needed later) must go through Express routes that
# authorize the request server-side.
#
# CampuSphere keeps Express session auth and the existing Google OAuth flow.
# Supabase Auth is intentionally NOT used.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=replace-with-server-only-service-role-key
#
# Optional - only if a future browser-safe read path is explicitly approved:
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace-with-anon-key

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEST-ONLY Supabase regression credentials  (M12.P1-R1; never runtime config)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consumed ONLY by the authorized QA probes and quality gates through the
# shared test-only loader (scripts/regressionCredentials.js) when a Supabase
# auth mode is exercised, and by the read-only pilot credential/session safety
# probe (scripts/pilotCredentialSafety-probe.js). They identify the four
# retained local-login regression accounts (admin, student, instructor, guest).
#
# Rules:
#   - Values live ONLY in the ignored local .env. They are never committed,
#     documented, printed, echoed in errors, exposed to the app/browser, or set
#     as Vercel/deployment runtime variables (server code never reads them).
#   - Supabase-capable probes FAIL CLOSED with a fixed sanitized message when
#     any of the eight values is missing or blank; they never fall back to a
#     documented or hardcoded live credential.
#   - Local MySQL probe runs do NOT use these: the deterministic local-only
#     MySQL seed fixtures (database/seed.js) remain the MySQL-mode credentials.
#
# SUPABASE_REGRESSION_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# SUPABASE_REGRESSION_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# SUPABASE_REGRESSION_STUDENT_EMAIL=
# SUPABASE_REGRESSION_STUDENT_PASSWORD=
# SUPABASE_REGRESSION_INSTRUCTOR_EMAIL=
# SUPABASE_REGRESSION_INSTRUCTOR_PASSWORD=
# SUPABASE_REGRESSION_GUEST_EMAIL=
# SUPABASE_REGRESSION_GUEST_PASSWORD=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudinary media delivery  (Milestone 10; server-only)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudinary is the media-DELIVERY target for campus images and 360-degree VR
# panoramas. Database rows keep only delivery METADATA (e.g. image_url,
# cloudinary_public_id); the three variables below are SERVER-ONLY configuration
# read only by server code (config/cloudinary.js). The media path is LIVE as of
# Sections 10.4-10.6: image_url is validated by utils/mediaUrl.js (a safe local
# /img/ path or an https://res.cloudinary.com URL only; everything else is
# rejected), the CSP allows res.cloudinary.com for media delivery only
# (img-src/media-src, plus connect-src because Pannellum XHR-loads the panorama;
# NEVER script-src), the service worker may bounded-cache
# approved Cloudinary media but never caches authenticated HTML and never mirrors
# /img/vr/*, the VR viewer renders a sanitized Cloudinary panorama where
# configured and otherwise falls back, and admins can store/update image_url +
# cloudinary_public_id on buildings and VR scenes. cloudinary_public_id is
# admin/server metadata only and never appears in public/runtime responses.
#
# Leaving these unset is fully supported: the app keeps using the existing local
# /img/* and /img/vr/* placeholders and never breaks (local dev, MySQL fallback,
# and the Supabase runtime switches are all unaffected).
#
# WARNING: CLOUDINARY_API_KEY and CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET are SECRETS (and so is
# any signed-upload data). Never expose their values to EJS templates, anything
# under public/, browser/window globals, app locals, response JSON, logs,
# screenshots, or any committed file. The real values belong only in an
# untracked local .env and in the deployment environment — treat them like a
# database root password. CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME is PUBLIC delivery metadata (it
# appears in every https://res.cloudinary.com/<cloud_name>/... URL), but its real
# value still belongs only in an untracked local .env / the deployment env.
#
# Real asset upload and credential entry are OWNER-CONTROLLED and performed
# outside the app (e.g. the Cloudinary dashboard). CampuSphere implements NO
# browser direct-upload, unsigned-upload preset, Cloudinary Admin API, or SDK
# flow. Uploading the final 360 panoramas is owner-controlled asset work
# (validated at the Milestone 10 end-to-end gate), not an app feature.
#
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your-cloudinary-cloud-name
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=replace-with-server-only-api-key
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=replace-with-server-only-api-secret

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel fail-closed production profile  (M12.P1-R2)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERCEL is a PLATFORM-PROVIDED indicator: the Vercel runtime sets VERCEL=1
# automatically. Never set it manually for local development.
#
# When VERCEL=1, server.js runs a PURE synchronous preflight
# (config/vercelProductionProfile.js) against the PLATFORM-INJECTED
# process.env BEFORE dotenv runs — an accidentally packaged repository .env
# can therefore never backfill a missing or misspelled Vercel Project
# variable — and before any backend client, session configuration/store,
# middleware, controller, or route is imported. dotenv loads quietly only
# after the preflight succeeds (or no-ops outside Vercel), keeping local
# development unchanged. The preflight requires EXACTLY the Supabase-only matrix
# below; anything missing, blank, misspelled, or conflicting makes startup
# refuse with ONE fixed sanitized message (the offending setting name and
# value are never echoed). Vercel can therefore never fall back to MySQL,
# Leaflet, or memory sessions. Outside Vercel nothing changes: the documented
# MySQL/Leaflet/local-development defaults above remain authoritative.
#
# Required on Vercel (set in Project Settings -> Environment Variables;
# placeholders shown — real values are never committed):
#   NODE_ENV=production
#   SESSION_STORE=supabase
#   AUTH_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
#   CONTENT_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
#   BUILDING_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
#   ROUTE_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
#   VR_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
#   SCHEDULE_DATA_SOURCE=supabase
#   MAP_RENDERER=maplibre
#   SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=  (real SERVER-ONLY Supabase secret)
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://YOUR-DATABASE.upstash.io
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=  (real SERVER-ONLY Upstash REST token)
#   RATE_LIMIT_KEY_SECRET=  (>= 32 characters, server-only, random)
#
# SUPABASE_URL must parse as HTTPS with a hostname and must not embed a URL
# username/password. SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY must match one of the two
# official SERVER-ONLY key families, by shape:
#   1. an opaque secret key: sb_secret_ followed by at least 20 characters
#      from [A-Za-z0-9_-]; or
#   2. a legacy three-segment JWT whose decoded header has alg exactly HS256
#      and whose decoded payload has role exactly service_role.
# Everything else is rejected: documented placeholders, browser/publishable
# keys (sb_publishable_..., sb_anon_..., case-insensitive), generic or short
# strings, malformed JWTs, and JWTs whose role is anon/authenticated/missing.
# JWT decoding is SHAPE validation only — no signature verification, no
# network request, and no logging of claims; live Supabase connectivity and
# session-store readiness are verified separately at startup/bootstrap.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared rate-limit store — VERCEL ONLY  (M12.P1-R4)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required ONLY when VERCEL=1, and validated by the SAME pure preflight above
# with the SAME single fixed sanitized refusal (which variable was wrong is
# never disclosed, and no supplied value is ever echoed). Local development,
# Docker rehearsal, and the test suites need none of these: they keep the
# in-memory adapter.
#
# Dependency: @upstash/redis, pinned to EXACTLY 1.38.0 (no caret/range).
# Anonymous SDK telemetry is disabled via the documented `enableTelemetry:
# false` constructor option.
#
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL
#     Server-only HTTPS REST endpoint. Must parse as HTTPS with a hostname and
#     must NOT embed a URL username/password (credentials belong in the token
#     variable). No live connection is attempted during the preflight.
#
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN
#     Server-only REST token. Must be nonblank and must not be a documented
#     placeholder.
#
#   RATE_LIMIT_KEY_SECRET
#     Server-only HMAC key, AT LEAST 32 characters after trimming, and never a
#     documented placeholder. It keys the HMAC-SHA-256 that turns request
#     identity into an opaque bucket id, so a short or published value would
#     make stored digests guessable. It is NOT a session secret and must not
#     be reused from SESSION_SECRET.
#
# Privacy contract: only an HMAC-SHA-256 digest is ever persisted. Redis keys
# are `csrl:v1:<scope>:<digest>` and Redis values are a bare integer counter.
# Raw IP addresses, emails, user IDs, cookies, session IDs, tokens, secrets,
# and submitted content are NEVER written to a key, a value, or a log.
#
# Fail-closed: on Vercel, missing configuration is refused at startup, and an
# unreachable store, a rejected command, or a malformed reply returns ONE fixed
# sanitized 503 with `Cache-Control: no-store`. It NEVER silently falls back to
# a process-local Map, because that would silently restore the multiplied
# per-instance limit this section exists to remove.
#
# None of these three values is exposed to EJS, public/, browser globals,
# application responses, logs, screenshots, or commits.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://YOUR-DATABASE.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=replace-with-server-only-upstash-rest-token
# RATE_LIMIT_KEY_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-server-only-rate-limit-key-secret
